Still 1.2.0. Pocket mode now says what it is — and notices a headset on Android.

"How to use it" in Settings opens four cards: what the mode is for, the three taps, the locked screen, and the sounds to ride by. A question mark in the pocket panel opens the same four, so they can be read again rather than once on the way in.

On Android, a headset arriving or dropping no longer leaves pocket mode in the wrong half of itself.
